1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:02,640
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,557
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:07,217
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:10,476
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,955
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,400
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,020
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:24,217
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,377
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:29,580
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:35,240
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:40,420
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:42,660
One Piece.

15
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:52,557
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:55,237
Your heart will be your guide.

17
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:58,477
Raise the sails and take the helm.

18
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,117
That legendary place.

19
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,877
That the end of the map reveals.

20
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:06,697
Is only legendary.

21
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:10,097
Until someone proves it real.

22
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:14,417
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times.

23
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,797
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

24
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:21,217
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:24,240
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:28,217
So come aboard and bring along.

27
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,600
All your hopes and dreams.

28
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:33,837
Together we will find everything.

29
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:35,960
That we're looking for.

30
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:39,677
There's always room for you.

31
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,400
If you want to be my friend.

32
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,840
We are, we are on the cruise.

33
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,700
We are.

34
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:58,397
Okay, at daybreak, the pirates will be
landing at this shore to begin their attack.

35
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:02,877
But the only way they'll be able to get
to the village is to go up this slope.

36
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:06,757
The rest of the shoreline is sheer
cliffs, so they have to come through here.

37
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,597
If we can fight them while they're
funneled into that narrow pass,

38
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:12,657
their numbers won't mean anything
and the village will be protected.

39
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:14,505
All right, sounds pretty easy.

40
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:17,457
Talking about it is, but
victory depends on our strength.

41
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:19,128
What is it you guys can do?

42
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:22,040
I cut. I stretch! I steal.

43
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:23,300
I hide.

44
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,504
We're trying to get in a fight!

45
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,894
Just make it up funny!

46
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,180
Come on, calm down!

47
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:34,100
Ah, Klahadore, welcome back. How is she?

48
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:35,980
She's resting just now.

49
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:37,632
She was quite exhausted.

50
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,697
I leave town for a few hours
to tend to some errands,

51
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:44,604
and everything falls to pieces.

52
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:47,477
That Usopp certainly knows how
to cause trouble, doesn't he?

53
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:52,325
Yes, and on top of everything else he's
done today, He claimed you were a pirate.

54
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:55,160
I can't think of a more outrageous lie.

55
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:00,450
Indeed.

56
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,220
What's this here?

57
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:09,157
Well, that's a present, of course,
from Miss Kaya to you, Klahadore.

58
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,577
It's been three years since
you came to this mansion,

59
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:14,517
and this gift is to say
thank you for your hard work.

60
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,877
It's a commemoration of sorts. How nice.

61
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:20,597
The glasses you're wearing are always
slipping and you have to push them back up.

62
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:23,357
So the lady of the house custom
ordered a new pair for you!

63
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:27,146
Isn't she just the most thoughtful
young woman you've ever met?

64
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:31,017
How appropriate?

65
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:33,760
Tomorrow will be a day
worth commemorating.

66
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:42,100
it's a crescent moon tonight.

67
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:44,150
Huh?

68
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:47,980
It's on nights like these
that I truly feel alive.

69
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:51,900
My heart races and my
blood boils in my veins.

70
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,497
Clorador, what are you doing?

71
00:03:57,580 --> 00:04:00,698
Why would you do such a
thing to Miss Kaya's present?

72
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:03,400
Oh, I'll be receiving a gift, all right.

73
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:05,340
But it won't be glasses.

74
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,440
It'll be her entire estate.

75
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:11,057
What are you saying?

76
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:14,700
I suppose there's no reason to
carry on the act any longer.

77
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:19,520
In a few hours, the village will
be mourning the unforeseen tragedy.

78
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:27,520
Three long years I've
quietly waited for this.

79
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:29,130
Miss!

80
00:04:29,213 --> 00:04:30,043
You have to get out of here!

81
00:04:30,126 --> 00:04:30,956
Run!

82
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,080
Captain Django!

83
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:53,400
Captain Django, it's almost daybreak.

84
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,012
It's time to get moving.

85
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:57,754
Good morning, Captain.

86
00:04:57,960 --> 00:04:59,019
Good morning, sir.

87
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:01,560
You idiot.

88
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:04,897
Only the sun can wake me up
and live to tell about it.

89
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:06,333
Do I make myself clear?

90
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:08,049
He's in a really bad mood.

91
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,557
Mornings are the worst. Just look.

92
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:13,934
The moon is still up, so the
sun couldn't have woken me.

93
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:15,886
Now, which one of you did it?

94
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,320
No apologies, sir.

95
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:18,774
We're very sorry, sir.

96
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:24,360
Good morning, gentlemen.

97
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,317
Wait, what's going on here?

98
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,957
He was mad just a second ago.

99
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:28,870
So what?

100
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:32,157
He's in a better mood now, and that's all
that matters, so keep your big trap shut.

101
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:33,160
Attention, men.

102
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:35,680
Let's set sail!

103
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:43,999
Yep, I'm a genius.

104
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:47,637
There's no way they'll be able
to make it up this slope now.

105
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:51,657
All this oil we put here should keep them
occupied while we go to work on them.

106
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:54,537
They're going to be busy slipping and
sliding around like a bunch of idiots,

107
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:57,267
and we show up and beat
the crap out of them.

108
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,397
Wow, so that's your plan, huh?

109
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,310
That's right.

110
00:06:00,393 --> 00:06:02,937
I'm going to defend the village
no matter what it takes.

111
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:06,137
Let's just hope none of us slip on that
oil and end up down there with them,

112
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:08,577
because that would be like
sliding into a meat grinder.

113
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:10,540
Lusop, I gotta hand it to you.

114
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:12,816
You're pretty good at fighting dirty.

115
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:14,160
Of course I am!

116
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:16,497
There isn't anyone alive
who can best me with a

117
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:19,521
slingshot or beat me at
the art of fighting dirty!

118
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,177
It's almost daybreak.

119
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:27,142
They're coming.

120
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:45,500
We're here!

121
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:47,860
All right, men.

122
00:06:48,100 --> 00:06:49,276
You know what to do.

123
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:52,560
Go ashore, crash the village,
head for the mansion.

124
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:53,660
Aye, sir!

125
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:57,200
Captain, there are already
two boats here. What?

126
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:59,800
Shall I investigate?

127
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,057
Leave them for later.

128
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:05,611
They don't look like treasure ships to
me, and we have a schedule to keep...

129
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:07,380
Where are they?

130
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:11,977
We were gonna fight the
Sun's up. What's the deal?

131
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:14,180
Well, maybe they overslept

132
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:21,240
Wait a minute, maybe I'm hearing things,

133
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:24,125
but it sounds like battle
cries from somewhere?

134
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:31,180
Yeah, I definitely hear them!

135
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:34,900
No, it can't be, what can't be?

136
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:38,168
There's a shore just
like this to the north.

137
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:40,670
They went...

138
00:07:40,753 --> 00:07:43,340
We're at the wrong shore? That's not good!

139
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:47,892
Well, this is where they had their
secret meeting, so I just assumed, okay?

140
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
We need to hurry!

141
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:51,737
Before they make it to
the village, where is it?

142
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:53,697
You have to head directly north from here.

143
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:55,697
If you run, you can make
it in three minutes.

144
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:57,777
The terrain there is
almost exactly the same,

145
00:07:57,860 --> 00:08:00,625
so all we need to do is
stop them at the slope.

146
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,260
Oh, no! Huh?

147
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:07,137
If those filthy pirates are at the North
Shore, then they've already seen our boats!

148
00:08:07,220 --> 00:08:08,617
They'll take our treasure!

149
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:11,440
I'll be there in 20 seconds! Aw, man!

150
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:14,366
My brilliant oil strategy
was all for nothing!

151
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:20,120
My precious treasure! Hey! Huh? What are
you doing? Let's get out of here! Yeah!

152
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:24,970
Help!

153
00:08:25,053 --> 00:08:25,883
I'm gonna fall!

154
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:29,020
Let go, you moron! Sorry!

155
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:41,140
Sorry, but you understand
the treasure's in danger?

156
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:45,200
That girl's gonna pay!

157
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:53,814
I swear on my life they'll
never set foot in my village.

158
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,057
That Luffy sure has a good runner.

159
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:58,617
He's so far ahead I can't
even see him anymore.

160
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:08,054
Those mongrels are in big trouble if
they so much as look at my treasure!

161
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:16,760
It's an ambush!

162
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:18,276
Somebody's up there!

163
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:21,080
We meet again.

164
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:35,840
I am the legendary Captain Usopp!

165
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,940
I've been waiting for you!

166
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,837
I wasn't supposed to
be the first one here!

167
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,637
He was running way ahead of me!

168
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,602
I can't handle these guys alone!

169
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,090
Crap!

170
00:09:55,173 --> 00:09:57,312
How am I supposed to get past this stuff?

171
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:02,680
The village!

172
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,136
That can't be right.

173
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:09,105
He said run north, and I ran in a coldish
direction, so I should be at the shore.

174
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:15,260
It's you. I remember.

175
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:18,357
You're one of the troublesome
brats who overheard our plan.

176
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:19,597
What do you think you're doing?

177
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:20,800
I'm warning you.

178
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,824
Leave here while you still can.

179
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:27,460
If you don't, my 100 million
crewmen will massacre all of you.

180
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,000
100 million?

181
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,534
Are we really supposed to believe that?

182
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:34,730
No way!

183
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:35,710
100 million?

184
00:10:35,793 --> 00:10:36,623
Incredible!

185
00:10:36,706 --> 00:10:38,137
Captain, he's obviously lying.

186
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:40,037
Then it's time to call his bluff.

187
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:41,296
They saw through it.

188
00:10:41,740 --> 00:10:45,380
That guy seriously thought he
could fool us. What's that?

189
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:47,913
You've been lying to us this whole time?

190
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,837
Captain Jango, take a look at this.

191
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:50,957
Oh, no, is it bad?

192
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:52,017
No, sir, it's good.

193
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:55,017
We searched those other ships and
found a huge load of treasure.

194
00:10:55,100 --> 00:10:58,617
It's hard to say how much, but I
bet it's around 5 million berries.

195
00:10:58,700 --> 00:10:59,530
What?

196
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:01,760
Five million berries?

197
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:06,186
How in the world did those guys
get a hold of so much treasure?

198
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:09,280
I see you found my loot.

199
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,437
Well, you can have it.

200
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,857
You're just going to let
us take your treasure?

201
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:14,770
That's right.

202
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:19,597
Just turn around and forget all about
this place, and the treasure is yours.

203
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:22,680
I didn't think people that
stupid actually existed.

204
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:25,486
At this point, he's just
embarrassing himself.

205
00:11:26,340 --> 00:11:28,720
Okay, do you know what a pirate is?

206
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:32,717
We're going to take this treasure, and
there's nothing you can do about it.

207
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:36,918
And there is no way we're turning
back until we get where we came for.

208
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,640
Well, yeah, that makes sense.

209
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:42,880
All right, then.

210
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:46,420
On the count of one, two,
Jango, you'll let us by.

211
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:49,576
It's that strange weapon from before.

212
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,637
One, two, die!

213
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:55,838
Why'd you ever try to get
my heart and treasure away?

214
00:11:59,580 --> 00:12:00,410
My head!

215
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:03,280
Hey, who is this crazy girl?

216
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,317
This isn't the time to
be hypnotizing yourself.

217
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:07,753
We got a mission to carry out, remember?

218
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:11,397
That treasure boat is mine, and I'm not
going to let you have a single bearing.

219
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,310
Do you hear me?

220
00:12:12,393 --> 00:12:15,417
In fact, you better clear out, because
I'm coming down there to get it back.

221
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:16,417
That really hurts.

222
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:18,137
Who said you could give them my treasure?

223
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:19,377
You got what you deserve.

224
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:20,817
I didn't give them the treasure.

225
00:12:20,900 --> 00:12:22,637
I just said I would give it to them.

226
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:26,080
That's the same thing and I
just saved your life. Huh?

227
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:30,817
I guess I forgot to mention it to you
earlier Don't ever watch his ring routine.

228
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:32,740
That weirdo's a hypnotist

229
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,687
Hypnotist, so where's Luffy?

230
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:37,857
He's a fast runner.

231
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:40,237
I thought he'd be here way
ahead of you I don't know

232
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:43,555
either got lost or he chickened
out at the last minute?

233
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:47,737
The only thing that could keep
him from a fight is getting lost.

234
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:51,077
Right when we need him to go
ahead and take command here!

235
00:12:51,160 --> 00:12:53,497
I think it's about time you
go and kick their butts.

236
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:54,410
What? Me?

237
00:12:54,493 --> 00:12:55,323
What about you?

238
00:12:55,406 --> 00:12:58,317
I can't take on a boatload
of vicious pirates by myself.

239
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,576
That's just suicide.

240
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:01,517
What, like I'm going to do any fighting?

241
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:04,957
Beneath this calm exterior lies
the abject terror of a coward.

242
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:06,717
Oh, so you think you're scared?

243
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:09,624
Well, I'm so scared I am
literally about to cry.

244
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:11,976
Please, your eyes are completely dry.

245
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:13,277
You'll have to do better than that.

246
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,477
Liars can smell their own.

247
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:16,077
That's just your upper lip.

248
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:17,137
I got beat up my...

249
00:13:17,220 --> 00:13:19,396
We don't have time for this nonsense.

250
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:22,297
All right, men, let's get to work.

251
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:24,439
Crush them and move to the village.

252
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,480
Here they come.

253
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:30,620
Wait, I know.

254
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:32,015
I have some Caltrops.

255
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:34,297
Those are just what the doctor ordered.

256
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:35,380
Let me have some.

257
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:41,980
You're gonna love this. Caltrop! Help!

258
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:57,293
Nami, if you're still alive when I get
out of here, I'm going to kill you!

259
00:14:05,060 --> 00:14:06,360
Take that oil!

260
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:16,057
Now, how do I get to the
north shore from here?

261
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:28,460
Which way is north?

262
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,400
Yes, we got him!

263
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:37,340
Check it out, here comes the lead star!

264
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:42,270
Bastard.

265
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:44,957
Way to go, you're quite
the warrior after all.

266
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:47,417
Looks like you got this handled,
so I'll just take a break.

267
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:49,500
But you haven't done anything yet!

268
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:50,730
What is it?

269
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:53,500
There are caltrops behind us.

270
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,070
Idiot!

271
00:14:55,153 --> 00:14:57,113
You dropped those things behind us, too?

272
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:59,100
Get out of the way!

273
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:12,758
Don't tell me you really thought you
were going to stop us down there.

274
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:15,557
Let's go, fellas?

275
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:17,500
Captain Kuro hates waiting.

276
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:23,857
You again!

277
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:26,157
Let go of me, you jackass!

278
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,480
You want some more?

279
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:29,297
Here, have some.

280
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:30,517
Have a little more.

281
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:31,800
I will never.

282
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:36,120
Let you step foot in that village!

283
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:40,680
All I did was lie like I always do.

284
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:47,477
See, today will be like every other
day in that sleepy little town.

285
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:50,137
Cause you and your cronies
will never set foot in it?

286
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:51,140
Shots?

287
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,060
Stupid girl

288
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:01,110
Treasure

289
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:03,410
Are you

290
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:07,200
Shut up, I won't tell you again

291
00:16:09,580 --> 00:16:13,577
We've wasted enough time playing
pirates Quit bothering with him

292
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:16,997
and move to the village Or have
you forgotten that this is Captain

293
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:20,537
Kuro's operation And he doesn't
look favorably on his well-laid

294
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:25,880
plans being ruined by idiots He'll kill us
all Do you understand that, you cretins?

295
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:26,890
He's right.

296
00:16:26,973 --> 00:16:28,564
Yeah, let's get to the village.

297
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:34,220
Don't go any further.

298
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:37,317
I said stop.

299
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:39,257
Turn back.

300
00:16:39,340 --> 00:16:40,837
Don't take another step.

301
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:42,140
Get off me.

302
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:51,757
Please don't kill them.

303
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:53,877
Just leave this village alone.

304
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:55,577
They're good people.

305
00:16:55,660 --> 00:16:57,577
They don't deserve this.

306
00:16:57,660 --> 00:16:59,377
I love this place.

307
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:00,440
Please?

308
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:18,557
What is this captain jungle?

309
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:21,157
Nobody told us the killers like those.

310
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:23,900
We're gonna be here about time.

311
00:17:27,740 --> 00:17:30,417
Is that the best those
pirates can dish out?

312
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:32,677
Yeah, I was hoping for a challenge.

313
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:37,637
And you— After leaving me down there,
you're lucky I'm not kicking your butt. Too.

314
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:40,600
You never told me which.

315
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:50,457
direction was north.

316
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:52,077
Who are these guys?

317
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:53,280
They're late.

318
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:56,540
I don't appreciate tardiness, not one bit.

319
00:17:56,880 --> 00:18:01,900
They know full well what happens to those
who are foolish enough to upset my plans.

320
00:18:08,620 --> 00:18:12,577
Do they think they can take their
sweet time well if they have

321
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:18,100
forgotten the consequences of
disappointing me I'll kill them all?

322
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:32,556
Wow, that was great.

323
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:34,602
You guys are really that strong?

324
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:38,977
Could you have been slower?

325
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:40,354
What took you so long?

326
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:44,317
You're the one who pushed me down
that oil slick so you could get out.

327
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,457
It was an accident.

328
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:46,617
I slipped, you fell.

329
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:48,897
At least one of us made it out of there.

330
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:51,337
That's better than both of
us being stuck at the bottom.

331
00:18:51,420 --> 00:18:53,240
It should have just been you!

332
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:55,057
Run straight north, he says.

333
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,057
That's just great.

334
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:59,297
I mean, how am I supposed to know
which way north even is out here, huh?

335
00:18:59,380 --> 00:19:00,210
Shut up.

336
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:04,137
You're the one who ran away so sure
of yourself, ready to take on anyone.

337
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:07,037
I just got so excited, I
started running, you know?

338
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:12,600
The sun rises high in the sky now, and that
means Captain Kuro goes very impatient.

339
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:15,777
Men, don't just lie there.

340
00:19:15,860 --> 00:19:18,177
You can't tell me you're
going to let them win.

341
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:20,142
They're just a couple of idiots.

342
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:29,101
The fact is, we don't have time to
lollygag around here any longer.

343
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:33,857
If our enemy is strong, then we
must become stronger than them.

344
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:35,940
Here, stare deeply into this ring.

345
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:37,520
Now, I will count one,

346
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:41,157
two, Jango, and after that, you
will all begin to grow stronger.

347
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:44,017
Your wounds will heal and
you will grow stronger still.

348
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:45,197
So what is he doing?

349
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:46,220
It looks weird.

350
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:47,900
Looks like hypnosis.

351
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:50,637
He's trying to convince them
they're stronger than they are.

352
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:51,838
Like, that'll work.

353
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:55,880
One, two, jungle!

354
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:01,080
No way!

355
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:02,680
Yee-yee-yay!

356
00:20:14,140 --> 00:20:16,840
That one guy completely
destroyed the cliff!

357
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:19,040
Now that's what I call power!

358
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:22,837
I always thought hypnotizing
people was a bunch of crap!

359
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,237
That was just one of them!

360
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:26,379
Imagine what the whole crew can do!

361
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:31,801
Now go, and strike down
all who stand in your way!

362
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,380
Hey, you guys, you might want to move.

363
00:20:45,780 --> 00:20:48,133
Luffy, you and I will take it from here.

364
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:52,177
All right, then.

365
00:20:52,260 --> 00:20:53,090
What now?

366
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,060
Uh, Luffy?

367
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:05,960
Don't tell me you let that
freak hypnotize you too!

368
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:15,280
Oh, he really is a simple-minded idiot!

369
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:36,780
Damn you, Captain Kuro.

370
00:21:37,020 --> 00:21:39,280
You made one hell of a miscalculation.

371
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:42,871
These are not your average village idiots.

372
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:03,620
Where's he going?

373
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:08,860
What is he doing?

374
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:19,780
That's right!

375
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:21,080
Tear it down!

376
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:24,800
He's going to destroy our ship!

377
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:35,620
Oh no!

378
00:22:35,920 --> 00:22:37,397
He's gonna crush us with it!

379
00:22:37,480 --> 00:22:38,500
Everybody run!

380
00:22:40,340 --> 00:22:41,170
Run!

381
00:22:41,253 --> 00:22:42,200
Captain, do something!

382
00:22:46,460 --> 00:22:48,980
One, two, jungle, you will fall asleep!

383
00:22:52,180 --> 00:22:53,417
One, two...

384
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:54,980
Jekyll!

385
00:23:29,460 --> 00:23:32,217
Looks like those guys are probably
down for the count, don't you think?

386
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:33,130
I guess.

387
00:23:33,500 --> 00:23:34,330
Maybe.

388
00:23:34,540 --> 00:23:36,737
But Luffy's still trapped
underneath that cat.

389
00:23:36,820 --> 00:23:37,650
Just look.

390
00:23:38,260 --> 00:23:39,640
Relax, he's fine.

391
00:23:39,860 --> 00:23:43,801
You should really worry about your
own injuries by the looks of it.

392
00:23:44,660 --> 00:23:45,954
Damn that little brat.

393
00:23:46,120 --> 00:23:47,897
Now our whole plan's shot to hell.

394
00:23:47,980 --> 00:23:50,156
What am I going to do with this mess?

395
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:55,220
Captain Kuro sees this and he'll kill us.

396
00:23:56,900 --> 00:23:58,457
Page come check this out.

397
00:23:58,540 --> 00:24:00,237
There's some bad stuff going down?

398
00:24:00,320 --> 00:24:01,800
What the hell?

399
00:24:02,740 --> 00:24:04,957
I forgot we still have our trump card.

400
00:24:05,040 --> 00:24:06,640
Come forth!

401
00:24:07,220 --> 00:24:08,320
Miyaban brothers?

402
00:24:20,840 --> 00:24:25,257
It looks like the butler from Kaya's
mansion, but it's so early in the morning.

403
00:24:25,340 --> 00:24:27,164
Why is he walking to the shore?

404
00:24:49,700 --> 00:24:51,577
Or someone could beat me?

405
00:24:51,660 --> 00:24:55,657
The promised land was in my grasp.

406
00:24:55,740 --> 00:24:58,320
And I wouldn't let go.

407
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:02,057
La la la la.

408
00:25:02,140 --> 00:25:03,457
My only dream.

409
00:25:03,540 --> 00:25:05,860
La la la la la.

410
00:25:06,540 --> 00:25:11,440
I won't stop chasing
it until it comes true!

411
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:16,960
But if the world ever changes?

412
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:30,817
As long as I'm with you.

413
00:25:30,900 --> 00:25:33,660
My memories won't fade.

414
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:38,980
Waiting for that one true dream?
